    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1225">

                <pb facs="0996" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2903.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-26T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Upon inquiry by the Mexican Ambassador regarding accuracy of recent press reports
                    published here stating that American troops are leaving for El Paso with orders
                    to cross into Mexican territory if shots are fired into the American side from
                    Ciudad Juárez or any other place, Department has replied that such reports are
                    without foundation, no such orders having been issued, but that troops are being
                    massed at El Paso as a deterrent to any such action by Mexican forces. You will
                    inform the Foreign Office that the Department has emphasized the absolute
                    necessity of Mexico’s taking such action as will prevent a repetition of the
                    untoward accidents happening at El Paso last year.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
